 {:db/id "q-81372" :question/id #uuid "cf817965-a661-536e-b9bc-f7b88632bc85" :question/math-academy-id "q-81372" :question/problem "$1$ is **not** prime or composite number.\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following:\n\n- $P:1\\text{ is prime}$\n\n- $Q:1\\text{ is composite}$" :question/worked-solution "The given sentence is the negation of the following sentence: \n\n$1$ is prime or a composite number, \n\nwhich can be expressed symbolically as $P∨Q.$\n\nThe negation is represented by the symbol \"$¬$\". \n\nTherefore, the given sentence is expressed symbolically as $¬(P∨Q).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-81372/ma-source-field/c1c4ccc94845abad1c93b4e6783c1ff134ba5ef122c4383cf62627335f410950"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
