 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "d578c6cc-9bea-57a7-8928-c304b5f6c737"] :question/problem "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola ${x}^{2}=12y?$" :question/worked-solution "The standard equation of an upward- or downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at the origin is\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nWe can rewrite the given equation as \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4(3)y.\n$$\n\nIt is now clear that our equation is of the standard type with $p=3.$ Therefore, our parabola has its vertex at $(0,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-84829/ma-source-field/ba8ac2e1498250f8444fc0328560f789a7a9930b27483d3a6ee5edb50276e745"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
