 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "137cbf82-f6fa-5b07-a735-e5850a186305"] :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=5x+6y,\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nUse Euler's method with one step to approximate $y(1).$" :question/worked-solution "Since we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=1,$ we will use a step size of \n\n$$\nΔx=1-0=1.\n$$\n\nFirst, we add the initial condition data:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ |  |  |\n\nNext, we compute ${y}^{′}$ according to the given rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =5x+6y \\\\  & =5\\cdot (0)+6\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add this to our table:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $6$ |  |\n\nNext, we compute $Δy$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(6)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $6$ | $6$ |\n\nTo get the values of $x$ and $y$ in the *next* row, we add $Δx$ to $x$ and $Δy$ to $y,$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx \\\\  & =0+1 \\\\  & =1 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\  & =1+6 \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these rows to our table gives the following:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $6$ | $6$ |\n| $1$ | $7$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(1)≈7.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-86975/ma-source-field/fda760b918986e5b5a4c7733e797099c6eac497ebcfec7037e315e19cb9a4d6c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
