 {:db/id "q-94268" :question/id #uuid "722a3581-8ce0-5ec8-baf3-aa06bcfd2a36" :question/math-academy-id "q-94268" :question/problem "The function $y(t)$ gives the position of a particle at time $t.$ Which of the following equations represents a situation in which the particle is undergoing simple harmonic motion?" :question/worked-solution "The simple harmonic motion (SHM) equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.\n$$\n\nWe can see that the only equation that represents SHM is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+8y=0.\n$$\n\nIn the above case:\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=8\\,⟹\\,\\omega =2\\sqrt{2}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94268/ma-source-field/37b465be270b63bcdaefe7386ea0a46da6fdf633a513e97704902e9334aa5587"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
