 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "25726fd8-78e9-529e-acdf-5c4c5a237b40"] :question/problem "Which of the following is the correct symbolic notation for the sentence given below?\n\n*\"The function $g$ maps the set $X$ to the set of real numbers.\"*" :question/worked-solution "The sentence *\"The function $g$ maps the set $X$ to the set of real numbers\"* is equivalent to the following symbolic notation:\n\n$\\,$ $g:X\\to R$\n\nHere, the domain of $g$ is $X,$ and the codomain of $g$ is $R.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-96040/ma-source-field/f30f5fbf17f70bb01ef9b475554c2ad1e4ea2f1df9ef5e44f745e9aecc176bde"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
