 {:db/id "q-96231" :question/id #uuid "eab879a0-3375-58dd-903d-5ef4248752b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-96231" :question/problem "$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\,∗\\, \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\,∗\\,\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $U$ shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ which of the following could be the second column of the matrix $U?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that since $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ the matrix $U$ must be a $2\\times 2$ orthogonal matrix. This means that \n\n- the first column must be orthogonal to the second column, and\n\n- the norm of the second column must be equal to $1.$\n\nAmong the given options, only the vector $[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{aligned}]$ has both properties." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-96231/ma-source-field/3b7ec209ab8cefcb1763c231cf2607c86367130cfbb363a005ae9f755a7130e9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
