 {:db/id "q-98768/ma-source-field/998a658c355779a56830765a9eee383875c63190736028c2571784ef17d90d9c" :answer-field/id #uuid "b3279ea5-57df-56e5-a59e-a9baf5354ec3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-98768/ma-source-field/998a658c355779a56830765a9eee383875c63190736028c2571784ef17d90d9c/003e03159af382809c52553d8c5103b1a8d7a1948ce3d500d5ff5b416e6167db" "q-98768/ma-source-field/998a658c355779a56830765a9eee383875c63190736028c2571784ef17d90d9c/a3a5487afcc81a1c06c56ceaee82744a099a79debc8be0e8469f77e68bf12a04" "q-98768/ma-source-field/998a658c355779a56830765a9eee383875c63190736028c2571784ef17d90d9c/4c22a7bc8e7836692695cb686ba405c69222960189c569b98a1356f01a46dcd1" "q-98768/ma-source-field/998a658c355779a56830765a9eee383875c63190736028c2571784ef17d90d9c/63fc6e544aa866b1c2116b59f1739ece133a8fa2f9217599b08f20fc5533117e" "q-98768/ma-source-field/998a658c355779a56830765a9eee383875c63190736028c2571784ef17d90d9c/b2bf59e36269bd39fbd388f126de8bbc8e28e7459d74c720f82ef1601a11e20e"] :answer-field/correct "q-98768/ma-source-field/998a658c355779a56830765a9eee383875c63190736028c2571784ef17d90d9c/003e03159af382809c52553d8c5103b1a8d7a1948ce3d500d5ff5b416e6167db" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-98768" :question/id #uuid "4670b2c4-578c-543d-913f-4a2e02949175" :question/math-academy-id "q-98768" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ which of the following could be the $3$rd column of the matrix $U?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if  $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of a $3\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ then\n\n- $Σ$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix with nonnegative elements on the main diagonal and zeroes outside the main diagonal,\n\n- $U$ is an orthogonal $3\\times 3$ matrix,\n\n- $V$ is an orthogonal $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFrom the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that ${\\sigma }_{1}=5$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=4.$\nAlso, the columns ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ of $V$ give us the right singular vectors of $A.$\n\nTherefore, we can compute the $1$st and $2$nd columns of $U$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute ${u}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we compute ${u}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we do not have the third singular value, we can't use the same formula to find the third column of $U.$ But we know that $U$ must be orthogonal. Hence, we must find a vector \n\n$$\n{u}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nsuch that \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0 \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0,\\end{aligned}\\,‖{u}_{3}‖=1.\n$$\n\nSolving this system, which is equivalent to\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{5}{x}_{2}-\\frac{3}{5}{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}=0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe get the nonzero normalized solution \n\n$$\n{u}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrix $U:$\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{4}{5} & 0 & -\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5} & 0 & \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-98768/ma-source-field/998a658c355779a56830765a9eee383875c63190736028c2571784ef17d90d9c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
